> Actual source diagnostics

These are captured source measurements, in original execution order. They retain weak results and explicit availability flags. Distinct tasks may use different reward scales; a smoke run does not establish convergence.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/external_envs_diagnostic0.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto data=dm::nn::load_npz("build/external_envs_source.npz");auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();int series=0;for(const auto&[key,t]:data){if(!key.starts_with("ale_enabled"))continue;auto y=t.to_vector<double>();if(y.empty())continue;std::vector<double>x(y.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);plot.lines(x,y,key,{37+(series%4)*50,99,235-(series%4)*50}).points(x,y,key+" points",{37+(series%4)*50,99,235-(series%4)*50},4);++series;}if(!series)throw std::runtime_error("source diagnostic missing");plot.title("external envs actual source diagnostics").x_label("Build branch").y_label("ALE available (0/1)").size(1100,600).save_svg("build/external_envs_diagnostic0.svg");}
